# Opalescence (turn 1), Humility (turn 3), Enchanted Evening (turn 5), worked out layer by layer (CR 613.1):
# - Layer 4: Evening makes every permanent an enchantment, and Opalescence's effect, though older, depends on it and applies
#   after it (CR 613.8a-b): every permanent but Opalescence is an enchantment creature. Evening's timestamp decides nothing.
# - Layer 6: Humility takes all their abilities (CR 613.1f): the lands' mana abilities (CR 305.6) among them, so no Plains or
#   Island of either player can be tapped for mana any more; Opalescence, no creature, keeps its own.
# - Layer 7b: Opalescence's part, then Humility's, in timestamp order (CR 613.7): Humility's comes last, so every one of
#   them is 1/1 - the lands and Moxes are 1/1 creatures and live, Evening and Humility are 1/1.
# Before Evening, the Plains taps for {W} (the positive control of the mana ability being lost) and Humility, an enchantment
# Opalescence made a creature, is already 1/1. Bot2's Island taps for {U} on turn 4 and not on turn 6.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Plains
Opalescence
Humility
Plains
Enchanted Evening
Plains x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Island x30

